# --- added 2026-07-24: private third-party conversation records. A transcript of someone
# who is not Luis must NEVER leave this machine in a commit. Privacy guard, absolute. ---
state/converse_*.json

# Private text must never be tracked. chains.jsonl records the GOAL of every chain, including
# private- and sensitive-zone ones; it was tracked until 2026-07-28. The writer now redacts free
# text for those zones (controlroom.chain_write), and the file itself stays out of git regardless -
# two independent guards, because a privacy failure is irreversible once pushed.
state/chains.jsonl
state/chains.jsonl.1

# Shadows are full checkouts of this repo created under state/ for testing a candidate version.
# They must never be tracked (recursive) and never carried into another shadow.
state/shadows/
state/proposals/

# AUDIO. Added 2026-07-29 while preparing the voice-session commit, after a check showed
# state/earcheck/ was NOT ignored and held RECORDINGS OF LUIS'S VOICE. His actual voice is the
# most personal thing this repo has ever touched and it must never leave the machine.
# The rest are generated artifacts: regenerable, large, and not source.
state/earcheck/
state/duet/
state/outtest/
state/fillers/
state/convbench/
state/_*.mp3
state/_*.wav
state/*.mp3
state/*.wav
voice/_*.wav

# The black box: audio + transcript pairs for measuring the ear from INSIDE. Luis's voice.
state/blackbox/
state/blackbox.json

# earbench. THE SAME LEAK AS state/earcheck/, IN A NEW PLACE, one session later - and it is worth
# recording why it recurred rather than just closing it. `--corpus` mode reads the black-box
# recordings and writes what it HEARD into corpus.json, so the output is a transcript of his real
# speech even though the module never touches a microphone. The privacy check was applied to the
# thing that RECORDS and not to the thing that READS the recording; a derived artifact inherits the
# sensitivity of its source, and derived artifacts are where that gets forgotten.
# earclips/ is generated TTS - not personal, but 100 wav files and regenerable in a minute.
state/lab/earbench/
state/lab/earclips/
state/lab/party/
# Persistent selves for the synthetic speakers - runtime state that grows every session, and the
# whole point is that it is theirs and accumulates rather than being shipped with the code.
state/personas/

# PIP WHEELS. Thirteen of these landed in the repo root from an offline install and were swept
# into a commit by `git add -A` - ~10MB of binaries that are not source and that pip can fetch
# again. `git add -A` is convenient and it is exactly how things nobody chose end up tracked;
# the privacy scan looks for secrets and had no opinion about build artifacts.
*.whl
*.tar.gz
state/council/

# R5's artefact store. DELIBERATE, not incidental - `*.bin` above was already catching the blobs
# by accident, which is not the same as a decision.
#   the BYTES are never committed: they are third-party content, not ours to redistribute, and one
#   dispatch writes up to seven of them
#   the LEDGER is not committed either: it is runtime state, and it grows every dispatch
# What this costs, stated rather than glossed: a third party can verify a citation only against the
# local store. Re-fetching the URL does NOT reproduce the digest, because pages change - which is
# the whole reason the bytes are hashed at arrival instead of being cited by address.
state/artefacts/
state/artefacts.jsonl

# ---- 2026-08-04: the entity's own deliberation is PRIVATE ------------------------------------
# `thinking.jsonl` is the rod's reasoning trace, kept from 2026-08-04. It reasons about Luis's
# actual employment and financial situation every tick, in plain words. That is precisely what the
# privacy guard forbids in anything pushed, and unlike code it cannot be redacted without
# destroying what it is for. It stays local, permanently.
#
# THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS COMMENT QUOTED THE PHRASE IT WAS BANNING, and the pre-push scan caught
# it in the staged diff. A rule that cites its own forbidden content publishes it. Describe the
# category; never the instance.
state/thinking.jsonl
# Experiment records that embed sandbox paths under the user's home directory.
state/armed_run.json
state/awareness_run.json
# HADES verdict text quotes the wake's own output, which quotes his priorities.
state/hades.jsonl
